  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Ellsworth</h2>

    <h3>Curaleaf Maine — Ellsworth (formerly Maine Organic Therapy)</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 3 Myrick Street, Suite B, Ellsworth, ME 04605<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 667-0510<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon–Tue 9am–7pm, Wed–Sun 9am–8pm (confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP cardholders) — OCP license DSP105</p>
    <p>Curaleaf's Ellsworth location is one of the original Maine Medical Marijuana Program dispensaries, operating since 2011. It was long known as <strong>Maine Organic Therapy (MOT)</strong> before Curaleaf Holdings acquired it and rebranded the storefront — so "Curaleaf" and "Maine Organic Therapy" refer to the same 3 Myrick Street location, not two separate stores. The brand's scale brings consistent product availability, with standardized strains, vape cartridges, and edibles carried across its Maine locations. It is the closest Curaleaf to Acadia for medical visitors who want a familiar national brand. Debit accepted; ATM and ADA accessible on site.</p>
    <p><strong>Visit:</strong> <a href="https://curaleaf.com/shop/maine/curaleaf-me-ellsworth" data-cta-id="cta-referral-curaleaf-ellsworth-guide" data-action-id="referral-curaleaf-ellsworth-guide" data-action-family="cta_navigate" data-placement-id="city_guide" data-referral-kind="dispensary" data-partner-id="curaleaf" data-referral-surface="city_guide">curaleaf.com</a></p>

    <h3>Main Street Medical Caregivers — Ellsworth</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 71 Main Street, Ellsworth, ME 04605<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 667-7703<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon–Sat 9am–7pm, Sun 11am–4pm (confirm before visiting)<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP cardholders)</p>
    <p>Main Street Medical Caregivers is a caregiver-run medical dispensary on Ellsworth's downtown Main Street corridor, serving registered patients with flower, concentrates, tinctures, and topicals. It is well-positioned for both local patients and travelers from the Bar Harbor / Acadia region making the trip down US-1.</p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="Acadia Gateway" type="passion">
    Ellsworth sits at the intersection of US-1 and ME-3, the two routes that funnel almost all Acadia NP visitors into Bar Harbor. For dispensary operators, this creates a built-in tourism channel: an Ellsworth dispensary can capture both Hancock County patients and the steady stream of summer visitors who arrive via I-395 and exit at Ellsworth's commercial strip.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Ellsworth's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Ellsworth is the largest town in Downeast Maine and the regional commercial hub for Hancock County. The town has historically anchored retail, healthcare, and government services for a wide swath of the eastern coast, and cannabis is no exception: with two medical dispensaries operating in town, Ellsworth is functionally the cannabis gateway to Acadia NP — the most-visited national park in the northeastern United States.</p>
    <p>Acadia draws roughly 4 million visitors per year, with peak summer traffic flowing through Ellsworth on ME-3 toward Bar Harbor and Mount Desert Island. The town also benefits from year-round residents across the broader Downeast region — including Machias, Blue Hill, Deer Isle, and the Blue Hill Peninsula — for whom Ellsworth is the nearest full-service dispensary cluster.</p>
    <p>Operators evaluating Downeast Maine should treat Ellsworth as the anchor market: a medical MSO (Curaleaf, formerly Maine Organic Therapy) and a caregiver network (Main Street Medical Caregivers) have both validated demand, and the town's role as a service hub for the surrounding rural region gives it a stable year-round patient base. Although Ellsworth permits adult-use retail, no adult-use storefront currently operates in town — recreational shoppers should look to nearby Bar Harbor (420 Mules) or the Bridgton / Fryeburg corridor.</p>
  </section>

